course: dictionary
lesson: 9022
title: The word sky
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A sky is the space above the Earth where you see clouds, the Sun, the Moon and the stars. It can also mean the weather or look of that space, as in blue skies or grey skies.
explain: Context tells you which meaning is used. «The night sky is dark although there are countless stars.» The word night tells you the author means the space above us after dark, where the stars are.
explain: Sky is a noun, and its plural is skies. Phrases such as clear sky and sky-high help you spot the word, and skyscraper means a very tall building.
explain: Looking at the sky can help you guess the weather. Dark clouds in the sky often mean rain. Never look straight at the Sun, even when the sky looks bright.
fact: Sky is a noun. Its plural is skies.
fact: «Sky» can mean the space above the Earth where you see clouds, the Sun, the Moon and the stars.
fact: «Skies» can also describe the weather or look of the sky, as in «blue skies» or «grey skies».
fact: The sky looks blue in the day because air scatters blue sunlight more, and at sunset it can turn red and orange.
fact: Never look straight at the Sun, because it can hurt your eyes.
exercise: «The night sky is dark although there are countless stars.» In this sentence, what does sky mean? | *The space above the Earth where we see stars | A kind of bird | The floor of a room | A sea full of waves
exercise: «Mercury is hard to spot, so it is seen only low in the sky just after sunset.» Where is Mercury seen? | Deep in a hole | *Low in the sky, just after sunset | Under the sea | Inside a cloud
exercise: Dark clouds in the sky often mean what about the weather? | Sunshine all day long | *Rain may be coming | The wind has stopped | Snow is coming in July
test:  Which is the plural of sky? | *skies | skys | sky's | skyes
test:  Which phrase describes the weather or look of the sky? | Skyscraper | Sky-high | *Grey skies | The sky's the limit
exam: Why does the sky look blue in the day? | Because clouds are always blue | *Because air scatters blue sunlight more | Because the sky is painted | Because the Sun is blue
